//! The `display` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets whether an
//! element is treated as a [block or inline
//! box](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Flow_layout) and the layout
//! used for its children, such as [flow
//! layout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Flow_layout),
//! [grid](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout) or
//! [flex](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Flexible_box_layout).
//!
//! Initial: inline. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - block: The element generates a block-level box
//! - contents: The element itself does not generate any boxes, but its children and pseudo-elements
//! still generate boxes as normal.
//! - flex: The element generates a principal flex container box and establishes a flex formatting
//! context.
//! - flow: The element lays out its contents using flow layout (block-and-inline layout). See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-inside
//! - flow-root: The element generates a block box that establishes a new [block formatting
//! context](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Block_formatting_context),
//! defining where the formatting root lies. - `table` - : These elements behave like HTML `table`
//! elements. It defines a block-level box. - `flex` - : The element behaves like a block-level
//! element and lays out its content according to the [flexbox
//! model](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Flexible_box_layout). - `grid` - :
//! The element behaves like a block-level element and lays out its content according to the [grid
//! model](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout/Basic_concepts). -
//! `grid-lanes` - : The element behaves like a block-level element and lays out its content using
//! grid lanes layout. Columns are defined by `grid-template-columns` and behave like a strict grid,
//! while items are packed in the block direction to fill gaps between items of different sizes. See
//! [Grid lanes
//! layout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout/Grid_lanes) for
//! details. - `ruby` - : The element behaves like an inline-level element and lays out its content
//! according to the ruby formatting model. It behaves like the corresponding HTML `ruby` elements.
//! - grid: The element generates a principal grid container box, and establishes a grid formatting
//! context.
//! - inline: The element generates an inline-level box.
//! - inline-block: A block box, which itself is flowed as a single inline box, similar to a replaced
//! element. The inside of an inline-block is formatted as a block box, and the box itself is
//! formatted as an inline box.
//! - inline-flex: The element behaves like an inline-level element and lays out its content
//! according to the flexbox model.
//! - inline-grid: The element behaves like an inline-level element and lays out its content
//! according to the grid model.
//! - inline-grid-lanes: The element behaves like an inline-level element and lays out its content
//! using grid lanes layout. Rows are defined by `grid-template-rows` and behave like a strict grid,
//! while items are packed in the inline direction to fill gaps between items of different sizes. See
//! [Grid lanes
//! layout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout/Grid_lanes) for
//! details.
//! - inline-table: The `inline-table` value does not have a direct mapping in HTML. It behaves like
//! an HTML `table` element, but as an inline box, rather than a block-level box. Inside the table
//! box is a block-level context.
//! - list-item: One or more block boxes and one marker box.
//! - none: Turns off the display of an element so that it has no effect on layout (the document is
//! rendered as though the element did not exist). All descendant elements also have their display
//! turned off. To have an element take up the space that it would normally take, but without
//! actually rendering anything, use the `visibility` property instead.
//! - ruby: The element generates a principal ruby container box, and establishes a ruby formatting
//! context.
//! - ruby-base: These elements behave like `rb` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - ruby-base-container: These elements are generated as anonymous boxes. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - ruby-text: These elements behave like `rt` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - ruby-text-container: These elements behave like `rtc` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - run-in: The element generates a run-in box. Run-in elements act like inlines or blocks,
//! depending on the surrounding elements.
//! - table: The element generates a principal table wrapper box containing an additionally-generated
//! table box, and establishes a table formatting context.
//! - table-caption: These elements behave like `caption` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-cell: These elements behave like `td` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-column: These elements behave like `col` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-column-group: These elements behave like `colgroup` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-footer-group: These elements behave like `tfoot` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-header-group: These elements behave like `thead` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-row: These elements behave like `tr` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//! - table-row-group: These elements behave like `tbody` HTML elements. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/display-internal
//!
//! Grammar: [ <display-outside> || <display-inside> ] | <display-listitem> | <display-internal> |
//! <display-box> | <display-legacy> | grid-lanes | inline-grid-lanes | <display-outside> || [
//! <display-inside> | math ]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-4/#propdef-display
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/display
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

module std.css.properties.Display.

